        "original_id": "8eec71d5-fbf8-5738-adb4-52c805c4edc2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Boleslawski, Herschell Gordon Lewis, William Kerwin, Allison Louise Downe\n- Films: Suburban Roulette\n- Roles: theatre director, film director, actor, acting teacher, filmmaker\n- Topics: splatter horror, wife swapping, suburban boredom\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Boleslawski, also known as Richard Boleslavsky, was a Polish theatre director, film director, actor, and teacher of acting who lived from February 4, 1889 to January 17, 1937.\n- Herschell Gordon Lewis was an American filmmaker who lived from June 15, 1926 to September 26, 2016.\n- Herschell Gordon Lewis is best known for creating the splatter subgenre of horror films.\n- Suburban Roulette is a 1968 American drama film directed by Herschell Gordon Lewis.\n- Suburban Roulette features William Kerwin and Allison Louise Downe among its cast.\n- In Suburban Roulette, the characters played within the story become involved in wife swapping to overcome the boredom of suburban life.",
